	<item>
		<title>AI agents now control part of Deepmind&#039;s compute for Gemini experiments, but recursive self-improvement remains distant</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/ai-agents-now-control-part-of-deepminds-compute-for-gemini-experiments-but-recursive-self-improvement-remains-distant/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/ai-agents-now-control-part-of-deepminds-compute-for-gemini-experiments-but-recursive-self-improvement-remains-distant/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maximilian Schreiner]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:23:36 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI research]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Short News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Google Deepmind]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=43305</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1600" height="893" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/gemini-4-neon__blog-header__sm.width-1600.format-webp.webp" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" /></p>
<p>        Google Deepmind uses AI agents to run experiments on their own for upcoming Gemini models. Research chief Koray Kavukcuoglu says the lab is still far from recursive self-improvement. For oversight, Deepmind intentionally leaves the agents' internal chains of thought untrained so they can be reviewed. Kavukcuoglu measures AGI by everyday user trust rather than benchmarks.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/ai-agents-now-control-part-of-deepminds-compute-for-gemini-experiments-but-recursive-self-improvement-remains-distant/">AI agents now control part of Deepmind&#039;s compute for Gemini experiments, but recursive self-improvement remains distant</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
					<wfw:commentRss>https://the-decoder.com/ai-agents-now-control-part-of-deepminds-compute-for-gemini-experiments-but-recursive-self-improvement-remains-distant/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
