					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/cyberkraken_4.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        The US Financial Crimes Enforcement Network took systems offline as a precaution after unauthorized access. Hours earlier, reports emerged of a separate breach at the CIA, NGA, and ODNI, in which investigators suspect attackers used the AI defense tool Artex. Both incidents land on a US public that is already on edge.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/back-to-back-cyber-incidents-at-us-financial-investigators-and-spy-agencies-follow-a-string-of-federal-hacks-and-outages/">Back-to-back cyber incidents at US financial investigators and spy agencies follow a string of federal hacks and outages</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
