		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[OpenAI]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=43274</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/openai_driscoll.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        OpenAI researcher Noam Brown is urging promising students to drop out, saying it's "not a great time to sit on the sidelines." The o1 co-creator says AI is still in a "centaur period" and struggles with planning and self-correction, though he expects a "very steep rate of progress" soon. According to Brown, language models are already being used to build the next generation of models.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/openai-o1-co-creator-noam-brown-urges-promising-students-to-drop-out-as-ai-enters-a-very-steep-rate-of-progress/">OpenAI o1 co-creator Noam Brown urges promising students to drop out as AI enters a &quot;very steep rate of progress&quot;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
